WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.321
Once upon a time there lived a donkey.

2
00:00:04.322 --> 00:00:08.714
His master sold herbs in the market.

3
00:00:08.715 --> 00:00:12.457
The donkey worked very hard each day.

4
00:00:12.458 --> 00:00:16.517
But his master wanted the donkey to work harder.

5
00:00:16.518 --> 00:00:21.325
Yet the master only gave him a little bit of food.

6
00:00:21.326 --> 00:00:25.342
The donkey was not happy.

7
00:00:25.343 --> 00:00:28.680
The donkey decided he’d had enough.

8
00:00:28.681 --> 00:00:33.188
He did not want to work for his master any longer.

9
00:00:33.189 --> 00:00:39.475
Only one person could help.

10
00:00:39.476 --> 00:00:44.836
The donkey searched for Jupiter, the god of the sky and rain.

11
00:00:44.837 --> 00:00:49.048
"Please give me a new master," begged the donkey.

12
00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:54.310
The donkey explained why he wanted a new master.

13
00:00:54.311 --> 00:00:59.588
"I will give you a new master," Jupiter said firmly.

14
00:00:59.589 --> 00:01:03.631
"But you will regret making this wish."

15
00:01:03.632 --> 00:01:07.847
The donkey was too happy to care.

16
00:01:07.848 --> 00:01:11.547
The donkey’s new master was a brickmaker.

17
00:01:11.548 --> 00:01:16.835
The donkey had to pull heavy carts of bricks every day.

18
00:01:16.836 --> 00:01:21.116
The donkey’s master wanted him to work harder.

19
00:01:21.117 --> 00:01:26.504
He did not give the donkey any food or water.

20
00:01:26.505 --> 00:01:30.985
The donkey was not happy with his new master either.

21
00:01:30.986 --> 00:01:33.652
He went to see Jupiter again.

22
00:01:33.653 --> 00:01:40.084
"Please give me a new master," begged the donkey.

23
00:01:40.085 --> 00:01:44.573
"I will give you a new master," Jupiter said firmly.

24
00:01:44.574 --> 00:01:48.885
"But this is the last time I will grant your wish.

25
00:01:48.886 --> 00:01:52.639
This will be your last and only master."

26
00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:57.389
Again the donkey was too happy to care.

27
00:01:57.390 --> 00:02:00.722
The donkey’s new master was a tanner.

28
00:02:00.723 --> 00:02:03.453
He caught and killed animals.

29
00:02:03.454 --> 00:02:07.639
Then he skinned them and sold their hides.

30
00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:11.191
This master was the worst of all three.

31
00:02:11.192 --> 00:02:14.713
The donkey remembered Jupiter’s words:

32
00:02:14.714 --> 00:02:19.438
"You will regret wishing for a new master."

33
00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:25.607
"Oh, it would have been better if I had stayed with the other masters," the donkey cried.

34
00:02:25.608 --> 00:02:33.858
"I may have been hungry, or I may have been tired from too much work, but this master will skin me like his other animals.

35
00:02:33.859 --> 00:02:39.604
He will make use of me even after I die!"

36
00:02:39.605 --> 00:02:42.889
The donkey learned an important lesson.

37
00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:52.390
If you are not happy in one place, you will not find happiness in another.

